# Everything is excluded first, then only what the build needs is re-included.
# An allow-list is the only reliable way to keep a stray .env or key file out of
# the build context -- and out of any image layer or leaked build cache.
*

!app/
app/**/__pycache__/
app/**/*.pyc

# Belt and braces: even if the allow-list above is widened later, none of these
# can be added back by accident.
**/.git
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.p12
**/id_rsa*
**/.aws
**/.ssh
**/node_modules
**/.terraform
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
